                                "sense_id": "b2c8d41c-fff2-34a5-8167-6e262600ebdd",
                                "text": "When they reached the foot of the hill they caught a glimpse of what might be rocks on each side—squarish rocks, if you looked at them carefully, but no one did."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e9ede339-5ed8-45eb-b26b-11baae990317",
                                "sense_id": "b2c8d41c-fff2-34a5-8167-6e262600ebdd",
                                "text": "The cars, which are of pleasing but somewhat squarish outline, are unstreamlined."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7bb23b1e-7d21-4837-b1f1-f512daf57677",
                                "sense_id": "b2c8d41c-fff2-34a5-8167-6e262600ebdd",
                                "text": "1996, Kenzaburō Ōe, An Echo of Heaven (1989), translated by Margaret Mitsutani, Tokyo: Kondansha International, Chapter 1, p. 22,\nShe gaily thrust her squarish chin toward the front of the tent."
